# gangbusters — "Gangbusters" (Quest 6)
#
# The player raids the trap house near the abandoned bus station, clears it, and beats the Trap
# Branch Manager into giving up the Mad Fisherman's name.
#
# GRANTED BY: Councillor Mosley's closing choice in quests/dialogue/councillormosley.quest, node
# wm_where — the same choice that completes wtf_mosley. Mosley's line there already points at "a
# little place near the abandoned bus station", so the hand-off needed no new prose.
# COMPLETED BY: the Trap Branch Manager's post-defeat choice below, which also grants Quest 7.
#
# ⚠ NEW KEYS: trap_house_gang (shared by every Roadman and Neek in the trap house — author them in
# ONE chunk, per QUESTS_AND_DIALOGUE.md) and trap_branch_manager (the boss).
#
# ⚠ THIS FILE OWNS THE TRAP BRANCH MANAGER'S CONVERSATION. He appears in no other quest, so it is
# inline rather than in quests/dialogue/. If he ever gains a second quest, move the whole DIALOGUE
# block to quests/dialogue/trapbranchmanager.quest first — one DIALOGUE block per npcId across the
# whole tree.
#
# ⚠ HE IS BEATEN, NOT KILLED. The design is that he stays on the floor in his final death frame,
# knocked out, and talks again. That works today with no new code, but it constrains the prefab:
#   - Health.DestroyOnDeath = FALSE, so the body is never destroyed. Health.Die still fires
#     OnDeath and awards XP before the early return, so the Kill stage below still counts.
#   - EnemyAI stops of its own accord — every one of its loops early-returns on _selfHealth.IsDead.
#   - HostileAfterDialogue.DisableInteractionWhenHostile = FALSE, or the Interactable is switched
#     off when he turns on you and can never be talked to again. The cost is that the talk prompt
#     is visible during the fight; picking it mid-fight opens a conversation with no valid choice.
#     See §"open gaps" in docs/plans/VAPE_ARC_BUILD_GUIDE.md.

QUEST gangbusters
TITLE: Gangbusters
GIVER: Councillor Mosley
LOCATION: The trap house, near the abandoned bus station.

# Stage 0 — the raid. Every Roadman and Neek in the room shares the trap_house_gang key, so this
# one count covers the lot. The count is a TUNING PLACEHOLDER: it must equal the number of keyed
# actors actually stamped into the trap house, or the stage can never clear.
STAGE KILL trap_house_gang x5
OBJECTIVE: Head to the trap house.

# Stage 1 — the room is clear and he opens up. Intermediate TalkTo: advances on the interact, which
# is fine — it is not the final stage and carries no hand-in.
STAGE TALKTO trap_branch_manager
OBJECTIVE: Right, that's them sorted. Better speak with this semi-important looking fella.

# Stage 2 — the boss fight, started by HostileAfterDialogue when the conversation closes.
STAGE KILL trap_branch_manager x1
OBJECTIVE: Scrap the Branch Manager, he's gotta tell you where those two are.

# Stage 3 (last) — he talks from the floor. MANUAL, not TALKTO: a TalkTo final stage completes on
# the interact, before he says a word, and would skip the reveal entirely (same reasoning as
# daniel_pauls_quest_one and wtf_mosley).
STAGE MANUAL
OBJECTIVE: See if he's more open to a conversation now you've split his domepiece.

# Not specified by the owner — 60 XP is a placeholder chosen to sit between wtf_mosley's 30 and
# ah_barnacles' 120. He pays in information, not cash.
REWARD
XP: 60

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Trap Branch Manager. One start node, branching per stage — a conversation has a single entry
# point, so his opening line is heard again from the floor. That is the same constraint Daniel
# Pauls lives with; if it reads badly, the fix is a second NPC, not a second start node.

DIALOGUE trapbranchmanager

NODE start
SPEAKER: trapbranchmanager
SPEAK: Oh man, that was a bit deep, weren't it? I'm just trying to get something started here.
CHOICE Where's Ralph and Sanjeet? Just tell me. I don't wanna have to do anything. -> tbm_subway
GATE: stage gangbusters 1
CHOICE You either tell me where they are or I take you outside and go all American History X on you, your call mate. -> tbm_beaten
GATE: stage gangbusters 3
CHOICE End Conversation.

NODE tbm_subway
SPEAKER: trapbranchmanager
SPEAK: Well, I can't tell you that. But just know, all this place is is a branch. It's just like a Subway. You're not gonna break up a Subway and ask for Mr. Subway, are you?
CHOICE Well, yeah, I guess that would work. But you're not a sandwich shop. You're a dealer. -> tbm_franchise

NODE tbm_franchise
SPEAKER: trapbranchmanager
SPEAK: Oi, I'm just a branchy. I'm just a franchisee. Come on, mate.
CHOICE Come on, just tell me where they are. -> tbm_fight

NODE tbm_fight
SPEAKER: trapbranchmanager
SPEAK: No. Fuck off. Come on then.
# No -> : this ends the conversation, which is what HostileAfterDialogue waits for before switching
# his EnemyAI on. The stage-1 TalkTo has already advanced by this point.
CHOICE Good luck fighting me in that suit you cunt! *fight*

# Reached only at stage 3 — i.e. only once he is on the floor.
NODE tbm_beaten
SPEAKER: trapbranchmanager
SPEAK: Well, I don't know. But if you go to the Mad Fisherman, he'll be able to tell you. The Mad Fisherman's the fella that got me on with them.
# Ends the chat, completes Quest 6 and grants Quest 7 from one choice — the same shape as
# dpq1_speed and dbb_chat.
CHOICE For fucks sake, if this is a wild goose chase I'm coming back you suit and ski mask weirdo.
COMPLETE: gangbusters
GRANT: ah_barnacles
